.TH SAPHIRA-ASSEMBLE-ROOTFS 8 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
saphira-assemble-rootfs \- build a complete Saphira root filesystem from a profile
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B saphira-assemble-rootfs
.I TARGET PROFILE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B saphira-assemble-rootfs
is the shared rootfs assembly path: the single code path consumed by
image creation
.RB ( saphira-image )
and disk installation
.RB ( saphira-install ).
Both entry points call this tool; neither reimplements it, so a
profile that builds a working image always installs a working
system.
.PP
Assembly runs six stages:
.TP
.B 1. Package install
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8)
installs
.IR PROFILE (5)
into empty directory
.IR TARGET .
.TP
.B 2. Machine identity
Writes
.I /etc/hostname
(default: the profile name, overridable with
.BR SAPHIRA_HOSTNAME )
and loopback
.IR /etc/hosts .
.TP
.B 3. System accounts
Runs the base layout's
.B apply-accounts
against the target with an explicit installer opt-in, creating
passwd/group/shadow from
.I accounts.tsv
and arming firstboot when root is locked.
.TP
.B 4. Trust store
Runs
.B update-ca-certificates
inside the target, mirroring the package builder's root
initialization.
.TP
.B 5. Root credential
With
.B SAPHIRA_ROOT_PASSWORD
set, assigns it to root via
.B chpasswd
(for automated boot-test images only; rotate on first real use).
Otherwise locks root with
.BR "usermod -p '!'" ,
leaving account setup to firstboot.
.TP
.B 6. Service enables
Reads
.IR profiles/ PROFILE .services
(one systemd unit per line,
.B #
comments) and enables each unit offline with the target's own
.BR "systemctl --root=/" .
Unit files come from the packages; the selection comes from the
profile. Socket cascades follow automatically through
.I [Install]
sections.
.PP
Requires root privileges throughout (device setup, chroot mounts,
target ownership).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT
Profile directory (default
.IR /usr/share/saphira/profiles ).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY
APK repository for the target; passed through to
.BR saphira-bootstrap .
When empty, the host repository configuration is used.
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_BOOTSTRAP
.B saphira-bootstrap
binary (default: alongside this tool).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_CHROOT
.B saphira-chroot
binary (default: alongside this tool).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_HOSTNAME
Hostname to write (default: the profile name).
.TP
.B SAPHIRA_ROOT_PASSWORD
Root password for boot-test images (default: empty, root locked).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All six stages completed.
.TP
.B 1
Any stage failed; the target is left in place for diagnosis.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Assemble the virtualisation host into scratch from a pinned repo:
.PP
.RS
sudo SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY=/out/stage4/packages/hatched \\
    saphira-assemble-rootfs /tmp/saphtest-root virtualisation-host
.RE
.PP
Same, with a throwaway root password for an automated boot-test:
.PP
.RS
sudo SAPHIRA_REPOSITORY=/out/stage4/packages/hatched \\
    SAPHIRA_ROOT_PASSWORD=test \\
    saphira-assemble-rootfs /tmp/saphtest-root virtualisation-host
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/saphira/profiles/
Profiles and per-profile
.I .services
sidecars.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-profiles (5),
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8),
.BR saphira-chroot (8)
